The firm profile leaves the agreement, and keeps its own page

"let's just delete the firm's profile" was answered too literally: the
page, its copy and its styles all went. "i only meant to delete it from
the retainer agreement." (JJ, 2026-10-09) Nothing had been committed, so
all of it is back.

What stays changed is the part that was asked for. The profile is no
longer bound into a fee agreement, in either the Word file or the browser
copy. A contract is not a brochure, and marketing copy inside one is a
second place to keep in step with Rules 7.1-7.3 every time the deck
changes, which is worth avoiding with a State Bar matter open.

What comes back is the page itself, at /admin/retainer/firm-profile, in
English or with the Chinese, with a print button. It is still the
approved deck's own wording cut to one page: something a person chooses
to attach, not something every client signs. Registered BEFORE "/:id",
because Express matches in order and a literal path after a parameter
route is never reached -- /admin/retainer/firm-profile would have
arrived at the draft handler as id="firm-profile" and answered Not found.

The agreement now names one office, West Covina, on the letterhead. It
used to carry all four twice: once in a footer and once in the profile.
check-retainer.js asserts the firm is still findable from the paper a
client signed -- an address and a telephone number, printed once.

